# Template for /opt/ds-staging/config/staging.env (chmod 600, owner deploy, OUTSIDE the source tree and the Docker build context).
# bin/init-config.sh creates it with random secrets; this file only documents the variable NAMES. Never paste real values into chat or Git.

# --- edge ---
# Since Stage 8C the proxy is the shared edge project (deploy/edge); its domains and IP gates live in /opt/ds-edge/config/edge.env (`deploy/edge/edge.sh set STAGING_ALLOW_IPS "..."`).
# STAGING_DOMAIN stays here for the watchdog; STAGING_ALLOW_IPS here is only the pre-cutover value (the old per-stack Caddy read it).
STAGING_DOMAIN=staging.sultonxoja.uz
STAGING_ALLOW_IPS=127.0.0.1

# --- database (compose builds DATABASE_URL; letters/digits only so it is URL-safe) ---
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# --- backend (compose pins NODE_ENV=staging, TRUST_PROXY=1, STAGING_ACCESS_GATE=edge, BOT_PAYMENT_MODE=MOCK, GMAIL_ENABLED=false) ---
INTERNAL_API_KEY=
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=15
MINIAPP_ENABLED=true
ANDROID_GUEST_ENABLED=true
GUEST_BOOTSTRAP_PER_IP_HOUR=20

# --- Telegram: OFF until a dedicated STAGING test bot token is installed with bin/set-secret.sh ---
BOT_ENABLED=false
# MINIAPP_ENABLED=true needs a syntactically valid BOT_TOKEN even with the bot off (initData signature check). init-config.sh writes a
# random PLACEHOLDER; replace it with the real test-bot token via set-secret.sh before BOT_ENABLED=true.
BOT_TOKEN=
# TAXI_BOT_TOKEN=            # second test bot; must differ from BOT_TOKEN
# Real taxi dispatch stays impossible: no operator has the Telegram id "0", so no company is eligible. Replace with YOUR OWN id for a taxi test.
TAXI_OPERATOR_ALLOWLIST=0
# MINIAPP_URL is intentionally unset: the bot's menu button is not touched.
